# EnterpriseStarter guardrails

| Requirement | Practice |
|-------------|----------|
| Backend boundary | Keep `apps/api` thin; platform code belongs in `apps/platform` |
| Modules | Implement `IEnterpriseModule` and register explicitly at compile time |
| Database | PostgreSQL through `EnterpriseDbContext` and shared platform migrations |
| Browser auth | Identity HttpOnly cookie, `credentials: 'include'`, and CSRF header |
| Authorization | `[Authorize]` plus code-defined permission policies |
| API contract | Application endpoints under `/api/v1` |
| API client | Shared native-fetch client in `apps/web/src/api/base/client.ts` |
| UI | Import **only** from `@/ui` (primitives + chrome); brand via `--brand*` in `theme.css`; features never deep-import or invent styles |
| Development | Aspire AppHost |
| Reference deploy | Compose migrator completes before API replicas |
| Secrets | Local environment/user secrets; commit templates only |

## Examples

```csharp
// ❌ BAD
await context.Database.EnsureCreatedAsync();

// ✅ GOOD — platform initializer / migrator job
await context.Database.MigrateAsync();
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
import axios from 'axios'
import { Effect } from 'effect'
sessionStorage.setItem('token', jwt)
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'
import PageBody from '@/components/PageBody.vue'

// ✅ GOOD
import { httpClient } from '@/api/base/client' // credentials: 'include'
import { Button, PageBody } from '@/ui'
```


```csharp
// ✅ GOOD
[ApiController]
[Authorize(Policy = ProductPermissions.RecordsRead)]
[Route("api/v1/records")]
public sealed class RecordsController : ControllerBase;
```

Do not add public registration, mandatory multitenancy, runtime module loading, or another database provider as incidental changes. Each is a product-level architecture decision.
